STIG Checklists — Windows Server 2019
Overview
This folder contains DISA STIG Viewer checklist files (.ckl) generated during manual STIG compliance assessments conducted against a Windows Server 2019 virtual machine in my cybersecurity home lab.
Assessments were performed using the official DISA STIG Viewer 3.7.0 tool against the DoD Windows Server 2019 STIG requirements evaluating Category I (CAT I) security controls consistent with DoD RMF methodology.
Files

Windows_Server_2019_STIG_Checklist.ckl — Initial STIG compliance assessment checklist documenting all evaluated controls, findings, and status
Windows_Server_2019_STIG_Checklist_Updated.ckl — Updated checklist reflecting remediation actions taken and current compliance posture

Key Findings

Evaluated CAT I security controls for critical vulnerabilities
Identified and documented non compliant controls
Remediated findings including Windows Installer elevated privileges, anonymous share enumeration, and LAN Manager authentication weaknesses
Updated checklist reflects improved compliance posture post remediation

Tools Used

DISA STIG Viewer 3.7.0
DoD Windows Server 2019 STIG
VirtualBox Windows Server 2019 Virtual Machine
